Nutation coefficients in src/generated/nutation_data.cpp follow the IAU 2000B
series as published by the IAU SOFA Board in the ERFA library (v2.0.1).
ERFA is a derived work of the SOFA software collection, copyright the IAU
SOFA Board, and is distributed under the terms of the ERFA license:
https://github.com/liberfa/erfa

VSOP87 and ELP2000-82B coefficients are from the IMCCE theories
(Bureau des Longitudes / IMCCE). Those series are published for scientific use.

The built-in Chebyshev series for Pluto, Chiron, Ceres, Pallas, Juno, and
Vesta is a fit to public NASA JPL Horizons state vectors. The fit is part of
this project. The underlying Horizons data is a public NASA product.

This library does not contain Swiss Ephemeris.
